<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI25-RBQA-F004>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI25-RBQA-F004" ;
  triage:title "resolve_peer_authority routing decision lives inside https_transport.rs, which peer-http-adapter.toml declares forbidden for recipient_routing" ;
  triage:description "Reported by ruthless-boundary-qa during AICH-S5-QA-2 (AI.25 fix-round-2 recheck, PR #640, commit 5f794c42). The peer-http-adapter.toml boundary policy (boundaries/atm-daemon/peer-http-adapter.toml:20) declares recipient_routing decisions forbidden inside crates/atm-daemon/src/https_transport.rs via io_forbidden=[\"...\", \"recipient_routing\", ...]. However, resolve_peer_authority (the routing-decision function for peer authority resolution added in sprint S25) lives in exactly that file at line 97. This function makes authorization decisions that route a delivery target to one configured hostname authority, which is precisely the type of recipient_routing logic the boundary policy forbids from that module. This is a policy/boundary violation, not a functional bug -- the implementation is correct but placed in a forbidden location. The finding persists across all branches s23-s26 (at varying line numbers due to forward merges and subsequent fixes). All worktrees remain open for this boundary violation." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "RBQA" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "workspace" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-26T12:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AICH-S5 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-07-25T16:26:33Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
